== 6.5 Chapter 6 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Incomplete records arise because a trader],
  [employs an accountant],
  [records each transaction once, if at all],
  [keeps a full double-entry system],
  [prepares a trial balance monthly]
)

#mcq(2, [In a statement of affairs, capital is],
  [liabilities less assets],
  [assets plus liabilities],
  [assets less liabilities],
  [the cash book balance]
)

#mcq(3, [Assets ₦600,000 and liabilities ₦220,000. Capital is],
  [₦600,000],
  [₦220,000],
  [₦820,000],
  [₦380,000]
)

#mcq(4, [Opening capital ₦380,000, closing capital ₦470,000, drawings ₦50,000, capital introduced ₦20,000. Profit is],
  [₦90,000],
  [₦120,000],
  [₦60,000],
  [₦140,000]
)

#mcq(5, [Drawings are added back in the profit formula because they],
  [are paid in cash],
  [are an expense of the business],
  [reduce capital without being a trading loss],
  [increase sales]
)

#mcq(6, [Capital introduced is deducted in the profit formula because it],
  [is taxable],
  [is a loan from the bank],
  [raises capital without any trading],
  [is a drawing]
)

#mcq(7, [A mark-up of 25 per cent on cost is equivalent to a margin of],
  [30%],
  [33⅓%],
  [25%],
  [20%]
)

#mcq(8, [A margin of 20 per cent on sales is equivalent to a mark-up of],
  [16⅔%],
  [20%],
  [25%],
  [30%]
)

#mcq(9, [Cost of sales is ₦240,000 and the mark-up is 25 per cent. Sales are],
  [₦280,000],
  [₦300,000],
  [₦320,000],
  [₦260,000]
)

#mcq(10, [Sales are ₦400,000 and the margin is 25 per cent. Gross profit is],
  [₦80,000],
  [₦100,000],
  [₦125,000],
  [₦300,000]
)

#mcq(11, [Sales ₦400,000, opening stock ₦50,000, purchases ₦260,000, and the trader's margin is 25 per cent. Closing stock is],
  [₦90,000],
  [₦40,000],
  [₦60,000],
  [₦10,000]
)

#mcq(12, [Debtors at the start ₦80,000, at the end ₦110,000; cash received from debtors ₦420,000; discounts allowed ₦5,000. Credit sales are],
  [₦435,000],
  [₦445,000],
  [₦465,000],
  [₦455,000]
)

#mcq(13, [Creditors at the start ₦60,000, at the end ₦75,000; cash paid to creditors ₦300,000; discounts received ₦4,000. Credit purchases are],
  [₦311,000],
  [₦315,000],
  [₦289,000],
  [₦319,000]
)

#mcq(14, [A statement of affairs differs from a balance sheet because it],
  [is prepared only by companies],
  [derives capital from a list of assets and liabilities],
  [is prepared from a ledger],
  [must balance by double entry]
)

#mcq(15, [Which record would NOT be found in a set of incomplete records?],
  [a trial balance],
  [a list of debtors],
  [invoices],
  [a cash book]
)

#mcq(16, [The best evidence of a trader's closing stock is],
  [the cash book],
  [his memory],
  [the creditors' list],
  [a physical stock count]
)

#mcq(17, [If the owner takes goods for private use, the treatment is to],
  [debit purchases and credit cash],
  [record a sale],
  [debit drawings and credit purchases],
  [ignore it]
)

#mcq(18, [Opening capital ₦200,000, profit for the year ₦80,000, drawings ₦30,000. Closing capital is],
  [₦310,000],
  [₦190,000],
  [₦250,000],
  [₦280,000]
)

#mcq(19, [A trader's sales are ₦500,000 at a margin of 40 per cent. His cost of sales is],
  [₦350,000],
  [₦200,000],
  [₦300,000],
  [₦400,000]
)

#mcq(20, [In the margin method, the figure usually computed first is],
  [the closing capital],
  [the cost of sales, from the opening stock, purchases and closing stock],
  [the tax charge],
  [the drawings]
)

#mcq(21, [Expenses paid in cash during the year were ₦90,000; there was an opening accrual of ₦10,000 and a closing accrual of ₦14,000. The expense for the year is],
  [₦114,000],
  [₦86,000],
  [₦90,000],
  [₦94,000]
)

#mcq(22, [Rent paid during the year ₦60,000 included ₦15,000 for next year. The expense for this year is],
  [₦45,000],
  [₦15,000],
  [₦75,000],
  [₦60,000]
)

#mcq(23, [Single entry is another name for],
  [a trial balance],
  [a computerised ledger],
  [a complete double-entry system],
  [a system in which only one aspect of a transaction is recorded]
)

#mcq(24, [A statement of affairs at the start of the year is used to find],
  [the opening capital],
  [the sales],
  [the closing stock],
  [the drawings]
)

#mcq(25, [Profit cannot be read directly from the bank balance because],
  [receipts and payments fall in different periods from the income and expenses they relate to],
  [cash and profit are the same thing],
  [a bank statement is not a record],
  [the bank makes errors]
)

#mcq(26, [Which item would be found in a statement of affairs?],
  [the depreciation charge],
  [the gross profit],
  [the loan owed to a bank],
  [the year's sales]
)

#mcq(27, [Goods costing ₦80,000 are sold at a mark-up of 20 per cent. The selling price is],
  [₦100,000],
  [₦96,000],
  [₦64,000],
  [₦104,000]
)

#mcq(28, [Using the last figures, the gross profit as a percentage of sales is],
  [80%],
  [20%],
  [25%],
  [16⅔%]
)

#mcq(29, [A trader's cash sales are ₦180,000 and credit sales ₦320,000. Total sales are],
  [₦180,000],
  [₦320,000],
  [₦140,000],
  [₦500,000]
)

#mcq(30, [If closing stock is overstated, the profit computed under the margin method is],
  [understated],
  [unaffected],
  [overstated],
  [always a loss]
)

#mcq(31, [The capital of a business can fall even when it makes a profit, if],
  [drawings exceed the profit],
  [stock rises],
  [creditors fall],
  [sales exceed purchases]
)

#mcq(32, [Which reconstruction is needed to find credit sales?],
  [the cash account],
  [the debtors' account],
  [the stock account],
  [the creditors' account]
)

#mcq(33, [A discount allowed to a debtor is],
  [cash received],
  [an expense of buying],
  [a reduction of the amount owed, with no cash received],
  [a loan]
)

#mcq(34, [A discount received from a creditor affects the reconstruction of purchases by being],
  [treated as a sale],
  [ignored],
  [added to the cash paid],
  [deducted from the cash paid]
)

#mcq(35, [The two routes through incomplete records are the statement of affairs and the],
  [margin method],
  [trial balance],
  [control account only],
  [bank reconciliation]
)

#mcq(36, [A statement of affairs prepared at the end of the year shows capital of ₦470,000. This figure is],
  [the total assets],
  [the closing stock],
  [the profit of the year],
  [the capital at the end, before adjusting for drawings]
)

#mcq(37, [Which is NOT a reason for incomplete records?],
  [the small size of the business],
  [the firm's auditor requires a trial balance],
  [the cost of a bookkeeper],
  [the owner's lack of accounting knowledge]
)

#mcq(38, [If opening capital is ₦300,000, closing capital ₦420,000 and drawings ₦60,000 with no capital introduced, profit is],
  [₦60,000],
  [₦120,000],
  [₦180,000],
  [₦240,000]
)

#mcq(39, [A trader's gross profit is 25 per cent of sales, and sales are ₦600,000. His cost of sales is],
  [₦475,000],
  [₦450,000],
  [₦150,000],
  [₦500,000]
)

#mcq(40, [The purpose of reconstructing a trading account in incomplete records is to],
  [prepare a trial balance],
  [find the gross profit and, with the expenses, the net profit],
  [value the fixed assets],
  [calculate the tax]
)

